        "body": "Part of divinevideo/divine-mobile#3697.\n\n## Why\nMobile share template is `https://divine.video/invite/{code}` and that surface is permanent (already shipped in app builds). The router currently passes apex through to `MAIN_BACKEND` (divine-web SPA), which has no `/invite/:code` route.\n\n## What\nIn `src/main.rs`:\n1. Add a new backend `invite_faucet` in `fastly.toml` pointing at the invite service (Fastly service `AG7CMNYuAbjxGVx9MtjhJs`, host `invite.divine.video`).\n2. Before the existing apex passthrough (`HostKind::Apex` arm), match `path.starts_with(\"/invite/\")`. Forward the request to `invite_faucet`, preserving path and query, with `Host: invite.divine.video`.\n3. No path rewrite needed — invite-faucet implements `/invite/{code}` directly (see the invite-darshan task).\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] `curl -I https://divine.video/invite/RX32-DXKK` returns 200 with `content-type: text/html` once the invite-faucet handler is deployed.\n- [ ] Other apex paths still go to `MAIN_BACKEND` (no regressions on `/`, `/profile/...`, etc.).\n- [ ] Unit test for the new routing branch.\n",
